    stem: "A swimmer is on a starting block at the beginning of a race. When she dives off the block until she resurfaces, the level of the swimmer relative to the level of the water is given by the function: h(x) = (1/60)x² − (1/4)x + 3/5. In the function, x is the horizontal distance in metres of the swimmer from the block, 0 ≤ x ≤ 12, where x ∈ ℝ and h(x) is measured in metres. Part (c)(ii): Use your answer to Part (c)(i) to find the horizontal distance (x), in metres, from the starting block to the point at which the swimmer reaches her greatest depth.",
